    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0478" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa,
                            Yokohama</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 16, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    prince of Satsuma has agreed to pay, within four days, the sum of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">£</hi>25,000 demanded by the government of Great Britain
                    as a further indemnity for the murder of Mr. Richardson in September, 1862.</p>
                <p>The demand for the surrender of the murderers has been practically abandoned,
                    though the prince has promised to use his efforts for their discovery and
                    arrest.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
